{"id":33169436998,"name":"Deliver dev candidate to onex-staging (OMN-15796)","node_id":"WFR_kwLOPuAjtM8AAAAHuQ1xRg","head_branch":"dev","head_sha":"25a24faeea8474fa0332411edb5cfaa634a1d037","path":".github/workflows/deliver-dev-candidate-to-staging.yml","display_title":"fix(OMN-16777): the consumer-flow reconciliation cannot use NOT NULL …","run_number":4,"event":"push","status":"completed","conclusion":"startup_failure","workflow_id":343376698,"check_suite_id":89889091093,"check_suite_node_id":"CS_kwDOPuAjtM8AAAAU7c6uFQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/actions/runs/33169436998","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/actions/runs/33169436998","pull_requests":[],"created_at":"2026-08-28T12:02:00Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T12:02:01Z","actor":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"run_attempt":1,"referenced_workflows":[{"path":"OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/.github/workflows/build-and-push-migrate-image.yml@25a24faeea8474fa0332411edb5cfaa634a1d037","sha":"25a24faeea8474fa0332411edb5cfaa634a1d037","ref":"refs/heads/dev"},{"path":"OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/.github/workflows/build-workspace-candidate-runtime.yml@25a24faeea8474fa0332411edb5cfaa634a1d037","sha":"25a24faeea8474fa0332411edb5cfaa634a1d037","ref":"refs/heads/dev"}],"run_started_at":"2026-08-28T12:02:00Z","triggering_actor":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/actions/runs/33169436998/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/actions/runs/33169436998/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/check-suites/89889091093","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/actions/runs/33169436998/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/actions/runs/33169436998/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/actions/runs/33169436998/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/actions/workflows/343376698","head_commit":{"id":"25a24faeea8474fa0332411edb5cfaa634a1d037","tree_id":"17dc3aa18e266f4e870a4abc40f445d7b88a2b74","message":"fix(OMN-16777): the consumer-flow reconciliation cannot use NOT NULL — it fails the very path it guards (#2956)\n\n#2955 (OMN-16773) made tests/ci/test_node_migration_shape_reconciliation.py\ngreen on node_projection_consumer_flow by adding guarded ADD COLUMNs to 0000 and\na new 0001. The gate is satisfied. The failure class is not: every\ndeclared-NOT-NULL column was spelled\n\n    ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS <col> <type> NOT NULL;\n\nand PostgreSQL refuses to add a NOT NULL column to a table that already holds\nrows unless a DEFAULT is supplied. Against a drifted pre-existing table it\nraises\n\n    ERROR:  column \"topic\" of relation \"consumer_flow_windows\" contains null values\n\nand ON_ERROR_STOP=1 kills the migration Job there — the same deploy-stopping\nfailure, at the same point in the deploy cycle, that the OMN-15376\nreconciliation exists to prevent. The static gate went GREEN while the class\nstayed open, which is worse than the original red: the red was visible.\n\nProven by execution on the .201 dev lane (mutable dev lane, throwaway databases,\ndropped afterwards), not by reading:\n\n  * seed: omninode_internal.consumer_flow_windows carrying ONLY consumer_group,\n    one row — the exact drift shape the gate's docstring names.\n  * dev's 0000 against that seed: `ERROR: column \"topic\" ... contains null\n    values`, psql exit 3.\n  * this branch's 0000 -> 0001 -> 0002 against the same seed: rc=0, rc=0, rc=0,\n    converging to 14 and 7 columns with both pre-existing rows preserved.\n\nWhat changes:\n\n  * 0000 and 0001 — every guarded add becomes nullable, and both gain the\n    BEGIN/END OMN-15376 fence markers they lacked. Without those markers the\n    execution-half suite\n    (tests/integration/migrations/test_node_migration_shape_drift_omn15376.py)\n    cannot derive the pre-fix variant, so this file was silently outside the\n    RED/GREEN proof even after #2955.\n  * 0001's header claim \"Keep the applied 0000 bytes frozen\" is corrected: the\n    same change edited 0000 in place.\n  * messages_produced gets an explicit ALTER COLUMN ... SET DEFAULT 0, because\n    ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS ... DEFAULT is a no-op on a column that already\n    existed without one.\n  * The declared NOT NULLs are not lost. They are established by the CREATE\n    TABLE in 0000 on the fresh-create path, which is the only path where they\n    can be established without inventing data. This is the\n    node_gateway_link_health_write_effect/0001 precedent exactly.\n\nEditing two already-DECLARED migrations is what the OMN-16705 append-only guard\nstops, and its only sanctioned escape is a new-ordinal supersession landing its\nsuccessor in the same change. 0002 is that successor and is not a placeholder:\nit re-expresses the corrected reconciliation additively, so a database that\nalready holds these relations converges from its own ordinal rather than\ndepending on the rewritten bytes of either earlier file.\n\nRewriting 0000 and 0001 is safe because neither was ever applied. Read live\n2026-08-28: to_regclass() for both relations is ABSENT on the .201 dev lane, and\nonex_application_migration_manifest — the relation bootstrap.sql joins to raise\n'conflicting migration checksum in canonical node history' — exists on NO .201\nlane (dev, stability-test, prod, judge), so the node-migration ledger loop has\nnever run and no content_sha256 is recorded anywhere to conflict with. Both\nsupersession rows carry that evidence.\n\nGates: 226 passed across the shape, checksum-conflict, append-only, manifest\ndeclaration and node-discovery suites. The append-only guard is exercised, not\nbypassed — with the supersession rows removed it FAILS on both files; with them\nit passes. Ledger checksums refreshed for 0000 and 0001, 0002 declared, manifest\ncount 116 -> 117 with the reason recorded beside the number.\n\nTicket: OMN-16777","timestamp":"2026-08-28T12:01:56Z","author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com"}},"repository":{"id":1054876596,"node_id":"R_kgDOPuAjtA","name":"omnibase_infra","full_name":"OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra","private":false,"owner":{"login":"OmniNode-ai","id":209038818,"node_id":"O_kgDODHWt4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209038818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra","description":"ONEX Infrastructure repository with PostgreSQL adapter and comprehensive testing","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/r